WEBVTT

01:00:58.500 --> 01:01:01.518
the difference between
breach and betrayal.

01:01:01.542 --> 01:01:02.934
How is that different?

01:01:02.958 --> 01:01:06.601
I think instinctually, we understand
what that might mean in a relationship.

01:01:06.625 --> 01:01:09.893
And that said, that may vary
from person to person in a relationship,

01:01:09.917 --> 01:01:13.726
but how do you distinguish
between the two in the workplace?

01:01:13.750 --> 01:01:16.000
How do those look different
in the workplace?

01:01:16.917 --> 01:01:18.643
AG: When I think about this at work,

01:01:18.667 --> 01:01:22.643
I think about what's called
the psychological contract.

01:01:22.667 --> 01:01:24.059
So all of you who have jobs,

01:01:24.083 --> 01:01:26.351
you have formal contracts
with your employers.

01:01:26.375 --> 01:01:29.184
There's also the what's called
the psychological contract,

01:01:29.208 --> 01:01:32.184
which is an unwritten set
of expectations and obligations